From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:40:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] kk: Declare SSA values in the innermost loop using them

Metal's compiler mishandles simdgroup functions on values held in
variables declared outside the loop that computes them. In a waterfall
loop such as

   while (true) {
      first = simd_broadcast_first(v);
      if (v == first) { r = simd_sum(v); break; }
   }

it runs the breaking branch with every thread of the simdgroup active,
as if after the loop, so the sum covers all of them. The same code with
first declared inside the loop works. nir_to_msl declared every SSA value
at the top of the function, so every such loop hit this.

Declare each SSA value at the top of the innermost loop that holds all
its uses, or of the function if there is none. vkd3d-proton's
test_shader_waveop_maximal_convergence now passes, as do its other 927
wave operation tests.

Generated-by: LLM
